1
00:00:00,550 --> 00:00:01,490
You can send a photo

2
00:00:01,510 --> 00:00:03,464
around the world in a second.

3
00:00:03,484 --> 00:00:05,184
So why can buying into a fund

4
00:00:05,204 --> 00:00:08,014
still take two business days to settle?

5
00:00:08,224 --> 00:00:10,324
Because the money sits in one place,

6
00:00:10,344 --> 00:00:12,004
and the record of who owns what

7
00:00:12,024 --> 00:00:13,195
sits in another.

8
00:00:13,215 --> 00:00:15,495
Different firms keep their own copies,

9
00:00:15,515 --> 00:00:17,745
and someone has to check they match.

10
00:00:18,053 --> 00:00:20,093
Redbelly is a public network,

11
00:00:20,113 --> 00:00:21,533
built in Australia,

12
00:00:21,553 --> 00:00:23,262
that brings the two together.

13
00:00:23,282 --> 00:00:25,618
Payment and ownership move in one step.

14
00:00:25,638 --> 00:00:28,235
If either side fails, nothing moves.

15
00:00:28,255 --> 00:00:30,285
Once it's done, it's final.

16
00:00:30,776 --> 00:00:32,374
And it's not a free-for-all.

17
00:00:32,394 --> 00:00:34,634
The people trading are verified,

18
00:00:34,654 --> 00:00:36,594
a bit like showing ID at a bank,

19
00:00:36,614 --> 00:00:39,124
and their private details stay protected.

20
00:00:39,358 --> 00:00:40,953
The rules are built in too.

21
00:00:40,973 --> 00:00:42,673
Before a trade goes through,

22
00:00:42,693 --> 00:00:43,393
the system checks

23
00:00:43,413 --> 00:00:45,335
the buyer is allowed to buy it.

24
00:00:45,355 --> 00:00:47,785
If not, it simply doesn't happen.

25
00:00:48,071 --> 00:00:50,651
So things like property, loans,

26
00:00:50,671 --> 00:00:52,111
bonds and investment funds

27
00:00:52,131 --> 00:00:54,731
can be issued and traded digitally,

28
00:00:54,751 --> 00:00:56,748
and settle almost instantly.

29
00:00:56,768 --> 00:00:58,798
People call this tokenisation.

30
00:00:59,203 --> 00:01:00,483
Redbelly grew out of research

31
00:01:00,503 --> 00:01:05,053
at the University of Sydney and CSIRO,

32
00:01:05,183 --> 00:01:07,804
Australia's national science agency.

33
00:01:07,824 --> 00:01:09,604
And when the Reserve Bank of Australia

34
00:01:09,624 --> 00:01:11,604
trialled a pilot digital form

35
00:01:11,624 --> 00:01:14,644
of its own money, in Project Acacia,

36
00:01:14,664 --> 00:01:15,844
Redbelly was one of three

37
00:01:15,864 --> 00:01:17,894
platforms that carried it.

38
00:01:18,165 --> 00:01:19,453
Verified people.

39
00:01:19,473 --> 00:01:20,725
Rules built in.

40
00:01:20,745 --> 00:01:22,116
Done in one step.

41
00:01:22,136 --> 00:01:23,486
That's Redbelly.
